kosha calculus-varga

  -- cluster for calculus quantities: derivatives, integrals, limits, series.
  -- calculus studies continuous change — how quantities vary with respect to others.
  -- kramanusara (derivative) and sama-kalana (integral) are the two operations.

  "math-varga-vishesa"

  -- sangati roots
  "kramanusara-swarupa"  -- calculus IS the study of kramanusara (rate of change)
  "kaala-yukta"          -- most calculus quantities involve change over time or space
  "seema-yukta"          -- limits (seema) are the foundation of calculus
  "niyama-yukta"         -- fundamental theorem of calculus is the governing niyama
  "viveka-yukta"         -- differentiation is the act of viveka (precise distinction) at a point

